{"type":"message","id":"5a098be1","parentId":"22c2434a","timestamp":"2026-06-03T15:52:14.860Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This path is protected too. The model catalog in agents.defaults.models is protected.\n\nThis is actually a significant limitation - the config system protects provider-level paths, model entries, and their properties. Adding a new model through config.patch is blocked by the protected path system.\n\nHowever, looking at the \"models.mode\": \"merge\" setting - OpenClaw's merge mode means built-in provider definitions are overlaid with custom entries. Built-in providers are loaded from the plugins. The minimax-portal provider has `models: []` which is overridden by OpenClaw's built-in catalog.\n\nActually wait - the issue is that `models.providers.minimax-portal.models` is in the protected list. \n\nThe real challenge here is that `minimax-portal` is a registered plugin with a dynamic catalog, so I can't modify it directly through config.patch. I need to find a way to work around these protected path restrictions.\n\nThe most practical solution would be to create a new provider entry like `minimax-m3` with the complete configuration, but that's also blocked. Since the model supports both Anthropic and OpenAI SDKs, I should explore whether adding it to the existing `minimax` provider (which already has API key and mode settings) might be the better approach, even though modifying that path is protected too.\n\nLet me reconsider - the protection likely applies to existing paths, so adding a new provider through a full config apply might work. The error about changing protected config paths suggests they're specifically protected for modification, but creating new entries could be allowed. I should try applying the complete config with the new provider included rather than trying to patch individual paths. I'm hitting a wall with the config schema approach here. Let me reconsider - maybe I should just try patching the minimax models path directly and see if it works despite what the schema says. That path is protected, but perhaps the real issue is just getting the syntax right for the raw parameter.\n\nActually, I'm thinking about this differently. The model uses the Anthropic API endpoint, and looking at the OpenClaw configuration, the minimax-portal provider already has this base URL configured. The provider is using OAuth rather than an API key directly, which might be the key difference - if the user's account there isn't configured for OAuth, that could explain why it's not working. I should check what auth profiles are set up for that provider.\n\nWait, I'm overcomplicating this. The config has protected paths which seem to be enforced at the schema level - these are likely built-in/registered provider paths that can't be modified through config.patch. That leaves me with either editing the raw config file directly with a restart, or trying a complete config replacement that doesn't touch those protected paths.\n\nSince `config.apply` only does full replacement, I should test whether adding a new provider that doesn't conflict with any protected paths works. Looking at what's protected - google.baseUrl and models[], nvidia baseUrl and models[], openrouter baseUrl and models[], zai baseUrl and models[], minimax and minimax-portal - I should avoid those. But maybe adding a new provider like `minimax-cn` with a different baseUrl could work. Actually, I notice the `minimax` provider uses baseUrl `https://api.minimaxi.com/anthropic` - if I create a new provider with a different baseUrl and a model ID that doesn't conflict with protected paths, that might bypass the restrictions.\n\nThe real issue is that any new model added to any provider gets protected, even if the provider itself isn't protected. The protection is at the model level within providers, not just at the provider level. So I need to find a path that doesn't trigger protection - maybe at the root level like `models.providers.my-minimax` where I can add models without hitting protected paths, or I should try adding at the `models` root level instead of nested under a provider.\n\nLooking at the error message more carefully, it's clear that creating new provider entries would also be blocked since the path `models.providers.minimax-m3` appears to be protected. Rather than continuing to test boundaries, I should just tell the user about this limitation and suggest they manually add the model through the UI or by directly editing the config file.\n","thinkingSignature":"c25d60b9fab44a82ff4a1f854eac990441ddd2f65e04b1cf43abe8b17c254d5e"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n路径保护的问题——`models.providers.*.models` 全部被保护，config.patch 无法添加新模型。\n\n绕过方法是直接编辑 `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`，你手动加一下：\n\n```json\n\"models\": {\n  \"mode\": \"merge\",\n  \"providers\": {\n    \"minimax-m3\": {\n      \"baseUrl\": \"https://api.minimaxi.com/anthropic\",\n      \"api\": \"anthropic-messages\",\n      \"authHeader\": true,\n      \"models\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"MiniMax-M3\",\n          \"name\": \"MiniMax M3\",\n          \"api\": \"anthropic-messages\",\n          \"reasoning\": true,\n          \"input\": [\"text\", \"image\"],\n          \"contextWindow\": 1000000,\n          \"maxTokens\": 131072\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n加完后在 OpenClaw 控制台（http://localhost:18789）重启 gateway 即可。\n\n或者，你直接在控制台的 Models 页面加，应该不受保护路径限制。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":142,"output":1087,"cacheRead":98368,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":99597,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780501912354,"responseId":"066f80994cacec61c1bc88d0a2e1fef7"}}
