{"type":"message","id":"9c9528b6","parentId":"c18512d6","timestamp":"2026-06-04T01:46:29.643Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The config was written but `lastTouchedAt` didn't update. This means config.patch wasn't used - direct file write doesn't trigger hot reload. humanDelay has `reloadKind: \"none\"`, so it won't auto-apply even if config.patch is used.\n\nHonest answer: I don't know for sure. The schema says `reloadKind: \"none\"` for humanDelay.mode, but OpenClaw's config system can sometimes hot-reload regardless of schema declarations. Let me test it directly with a simple reply to see if the delay is gone.\n\n实际上：\n\n刚才 schema 显示 `humanDelay.mode` 的 `reloadKind: \"none\"`——**这个 key 不会自动热重载**。\n\n而且我刚才用的是直接改文件（python），不是 `config.patch`，所以 `lastTouchedAt` 没更新。\n\n**两种可能：**\n1. 真的不生效，要重启\n2. 实际行为跟 schema 不一致，运气好生效了\n\n要不要试一发？这次回复如果没延迟，就是生效了；如果还有延迟，就得 `gateway restart`。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M3","usage":{"input":59,"output":216,"cacheRead":95929,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":96204,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780537578650,"responseId":"06700bebcd562dc21fdd7c3766004019"}}
